      "widgets_values": [
        "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 2D-animated Japanese anime style with thick ink outlines, flat cel shading, and hand-drawn impact lines, a low-angle medium-wide shot frames a towering moss-covered stone golem with glowing amber cracks across its chest as it drives its massive right fist down toward a young female swordswoman in dark leather armor over a pale blue tabard, her long silver ponytail streaming behind her. She pushes off the cracked flagstones and rolls to her right as the fist smashes into the ground, throwing up chunks of rock and a burst of dust. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at fast speed and shakes strongly on the impact as she rises out of the roll and slashes her single-edged longsword upward across the golem's forearm, leaving a bright white blade trail and a spray of stone chips and orange sparks. The shot ends with her landing in a low stance, sword held back and level, as the golem's head turns toward her.\n\noverall_soundscape: A deep grinding rumble of shifting stone builds as the golem's fist drives down, ending in a heavy concussive impact with rubble scattering across the flagstones. Boots scrape and fabric snaps during the dodge, followed by a sharp metallic ring as the blade bites into stone and a short exhaled breath from the swordswoman.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Fast tremolo strings and staccato brass at a rapid tempo, punctuated by a single taiko strike landing on the fist impact and a cymbal swell that cuts off abruptly at the end.",
